# START — Agent Entry Gate & Routing Specification

File: openOODA/START.oot
Work from this folder. All paths are relative to here.
This file is process, not product source.

## 0. The Five Invariant Axioms & Mandatory Laws

1. Negative Trust & Adversarial Verification:
   - Assume all stubs, docstrings, headers, and green passes are broken, deceptive, or hallucinated until proven otherwise.
   - Active Falsification: Prove fail-closed behavior by passing mutated tags, invalid inputs, and forged credentials.
   - AST Honesty: Scan for dummy returns, `destub` annotations, and fake pass flags (`scripts/std_qa/std_qa_honesty.oo`).
   - Double-Run Mandate: Always execute test suites twice to expose non-deterministic memory corruptions and ARC double-frees.

2. Ground-Truth Spec Derivation:
   - Derive algorithms, state machines, and data models directly from mathematical invariants and official specifications (RFCs, NIST KATs, IEEE standards).
   - Never mimic existing code or wrap unverified stubs/facades.

3. Fail-Closed Defensive Architecture:
   - Standard library and runtime operations must fail closed: zero panics, zero unhandled exceptions, bounded memory allocations, and clean teardown.
   - All standard methods return explicit `Result[T, String]` or clean fail-closed values.

4. Strict Sovereign Lane Isolation:
   - Maintain strict file-disjoint boundaries: do not edit compiler internals, registry, PM, LSP, or other agents' designated paths without explicit instruction.
   - Work strictly within your assigned module scope.

5. Zero-Orphan Full Lifecycle Delivery:
   - Never leave trailing TODOs, dummy return stubs, uncommitted test gates, or unlinked dependencies.
   - Every component must be end-to-end verified, double-run certified, and documented in SHIPPED.oot before exiting.

6. Mandatory File Type Law (Zero Tolerance):
   Only two file extensions are authorized in this repository:
     1. `.oo` ONLY — All product code, compiler, standard library, CLI, scripts, test harnesses, autofixers, tooling, QA runners, and code generators.
     2. `.oot` ONLY — All process boards, research papers, RFCs, documentation, specifications, and audit rollups.
     Generated `.oot` files are still `.oot` but carry `THIS FILE IS GENERATED — DO NOT EDIT` and are produced only by a pure `.oo` generator.

STRICTLY FORBIDDEN:
  - No `.py` — Python is completely unauthorized across all directories.
  - No `.sh` — except the two host scripts named below.
  - No `.js` / `.ts` / `.rb` / `.pl` (except third-party editor glue in `vscode/server/`).
  - No `.md` — All documentation, boards, and notes MUST be `.oot`.

Two host exceptions: `../ooda/bootstrap/oodac_pure_build` starts gcc and the seed compiler, and `../openOODA.github.io/install.sh` is the public host installer (bash, `curl https://openooda.org/install.sh | bash`). No other `.sh` or `.py`. `qa/e2e/*.sh` is QA-owned shell, allowed in `qa/` only.

## 1. The 10 Canonical Process Boards

The entire project governance is partitioned across exactly 10 process boards in `openOODA/`:

  1. START.oot     — Agent entry gate, routing specification, file laws, directory map, reading sequence, pre-modification gate.
  2. RULES.oot     — Immutable repository law, core principles, security baseline, clean code rules, planning constraints.
  3. NORTHSTAR.oot — Long-term architectural design, language grammar, AST structure, type system, and compiler target specs.
  4. MOONSHOTS.oot — Visionary paradigm shifts (OODA 2.0, metamorphic binaries, self-healing systems, verifiable compute).
  5. ROADMAP.oot   — Release pin, rebuild commands, closed deliverables, and later residual tracks.
  6. SHIPPED.oot   — Generated inventory of verified capabilities on disk. Produced by `scripts/generate_shipped.oo`. Do not hand-edit.
  7. FORMAT.oot    — Academy format, ASD-STE100 writing form, .oot structure, <=256 line limit.
  8. SECURITY.oot  — Capability security model and capability op matrix.
  9. WORKFLOW.oot  — Where to write, OODA tempo, swarm, probing, bug lore.
  10. QUICKREF.oot  — Universal AI quick reference: syntax, types, stdlib map, zero-trust verification laws.

## 2. Directory Map (Where Things Live)

Full write map: WORKFLOW.oot section 0. Short map:

  this folder            10 boards, audit/ (door only, see below), rfcs/, scripts/
  ../ooda/               Product: oodac/, cli/, runtime/, std/, scripts/, install/, docs/ (TOKEN_TOOLING.oot + AGENTS.oot), pm/ (stub, do not grow)
  ../qa/                 Hostile proofs — qa_master.oo (22 green) + pm_*_spine.oo + tests_* + e2e/*.sh (allowed only in qa/)
  ../openOODA.github.io  Public site: / door, /guide/ ops. /research/ is archive, not nav. Internal LLM: ignore completely.
  ../registry/           Public store: index, catalog, index.minisig, index.html

   ../ooda/scripts/       Pure .oo smokes, proofs, tools, and fixers — script_lint.oo enforces Academy headers
   ../ooda/fixtures/      Test fixtures and input files that smokes point at
   ../ooda/bootstrap/     Seed compiler, official rebuild, and check corpus only
   ../ooda/docs/          TOKEN_TOOLING.oot — use ooda outline/reflect/check/dump (~1.3% context), never cat ~/.cache/ooda-tmp/**/all*.c (~700KB) or full ROADMAP.oot
   ../ooda/AGENTS.oot     Hard traps — string index != 0 forbidden, "\r" ≠ CR, write_file needs OODA_FS_WRITEDIR, never copy bin/ooda onto oodac/oodac
   scripts/               Board tools — check_board.oo (10-board whitelist), enforcer.oo (forbidden ext + ≤256 + Academy + 8-gate), verify_all.oo (oodac check + SHIPPED freshness), generate_shipped.oo (live double-run hostile probes — forces code review), purge_audit.oo
   audit/                 Door: library_status.oot+22 siblings (GREEN/BLOCKED inventory). Gate: cross_ref_audit.oot (0 dead refs). Rollup: roadmap_ns_rollup.oot (historical). Ignore everything else — wave logs move to archive_2026_08_19.tgz.
   rfcs/                  Technical RFCs — copy 0000-template.oot (Status Draft→Active→Accepted→Implemented, Security & Capability Impact and Testing & Verification Criteria both mandatory)

`../ooda/bootstrap/` is not a process board. It holds:
  - `seed/oodac` — first trusted compiler binary
  - `oodac_pure_build` — the one allowed host rebuild
  - `corpus/` — pass/fail check fixtures
Do not add honesty-pack `.oot` files there. Residual truth lives in SHIPPED.oot (generated) and ROADMAP.oot.

`scripts/check_board.oo` must be run from this folder (`openOODA/`). It keeps the ten boards and deletes any other `*.oot` here. Do not run it from the repo root or from `../ooda/`.

`../ooda/pm/` is a stub (33 .oo files). Do not grow it. Real PM lives in `../ooda/cli/cmd_pm*.oo + ../ooda/cli/pm_*.oo + ../qa/pm_*_spine.oo`.

## 3. Reading Priority & Loading Sequence

Read only what this turn needs. Order matters.

### Always (mandatory run, not just read)
  The owner's ask
  RULES.oot — law
  SHIPPED.oot — what exists on disk (generated — verify freshness via `scripts/generate_shipped.oo`, do not trust blindly — run, do not read)
  SECURITY.oot §1-2 + §4 op lookup + §6 arg-flow — binary defense (Landlock, HMAC attenuation, rlimit, FsWriteCap + OODA_FS_WRITEDIR). Seals live in `ooda/runtime/chs_rt_caps.c`, not the historical `STATIC_CAPS.oot`.
  WORKFLOW.oot section 0 — where to write
  `ooda/docs/TOKEN_TOOLING.oot` + `ooda/AGENTS.oot` — outline|reflect|check on named files; never cat full ROADMAP or emitted C.

### When the work is product code
  ROADMAP.oot — pin, rebuild, section 5 Open this cycle. Section 6 residual tracks are later. Do not pick a section-6 row unless the owner names it. Open rows must cite RFC ID or `residual`.
  SECURITY.oot — full op table when adding/fs/exec/net/cap/HMAC/Landlock edits
  NORTHSTAR.oot — only if the design is actually in doubt

### Only when needed
  WORKFLOW.oot rest — OODA tempo, swarm (§2 Phalanx 12 agents, file-disjoint), hostile probing (§3, Double-Run Law CRIT), bug lore (§5 Lore 2 decoy offset, Lore 4 cap fail-closed, Lore 8 string traps)
  FORMAT.oot — writing a new .oo or .oot header
  MOONSHOTS.oot — long-term vision, not this week
  rfcs/0000-template.oot — RFC process Draft→Active→Accepted→Implemented (Security & Testing both mandatory) — wire via WORKFLOW §0 row already added
  qa/qa_master.oo — 22 green, run via `../ooda/bin/ooda run ./qa_master.oo` for product rail
  scripts/check_board.oo, scripts/verify_all.oo, scripts/enforcer.oo, scripts/generate_shipped.oo, scripts/purge_audit.oo, ooda/scripts/script_lint.oo

### Fence (do not cross)
  `openOODA.github.io/` is public — ignore it as ground truth; internal cross-ref is the 10 boards + SHIPPED + audit/cross_ref_audit.oot.
  `audit/plan1_*`, `audit/plan2_*`, `audit/plan3_*`, `audit/wasm_*`, `audit/x86_*`, `audit/win_*`, `audit/green/*`, `audit/research_paper_audit.oot` are wave logs and design specs, not gates — ignore.

## 4. Pre-Modification Gate & Axioms

Before you change product code (../ooda/ or related trees), say in plain English:
  1. Active goal — the owner's sentence, then which NORTHSTAR / ROADMAP item it serves
  2. Axiom — which RULES principle binds the change

No goal and axiom means no product edit.

Decide at most 5 work items per turn. Prefer one clear ship.
Then run WORKFLOW.oot (write map, then OODA tempo). Respect lane ownership in ROADMAP.oot.
  Residual ROADMAP tracks are not this week's work unless the owner named the row.
